{
  "baseline": "18424801. The intervening Word proof and Deck input changes do not alter the Sheet calculation or file format code. Both reference workbooks use synthetic inputs, with the controlling A1 cell set to 7 and 12 respectively.",
  "scope": "Eight stored-value IS predicates, ISEVEN, ISODD, TYPE, N, ERROR.TYPE and NA use first-party classification and conversion. ISREF and INDEX are retained as independent reference and reference-producer controls. The model remembers imported ordinary TYPE entry, legacy one-cell CSE and dynamic array modes through copy/fill/sort and reference rewrites. The XLSX checkbox mapping resolves bounded typed backward references and writes the mapper name accepted by Excel.",
  "independentReference": "Microsoft Excel for Mac 16.115 opened and independently recalculated the workbooks. JoySheet previously changed 47 of 176 TYPE entry modes in each file. For the old-writer reference copies only, the missing checkbox mapper name was added before recalculating in Excel, preserving the worksheet XML supplied by the old writer. Excel then produced 34 different results in each workbook. The original Excel files, both prior-writer reference sheets and the current JoySheet output are checked separately.",
